{{also|copout|cop-out}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Probably from [[cop a plea]]

===Verb===
{{en-verb|inf=to [[cop]] [[out]]|cops out|copping out|copped out}}

# {{idiomatic}} To [[avoid]] or [[shirk]], either by failing to perform, or by performing in a grossly [[insufficient]], [[negligent]], or [[superficial]] manner.
#: ''Faced with the prospect of actually having to work, the "other" firm copped out and passed all the work onto the firms.''

